From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: feature/gallery-round: send a gallery video as a video message

PhotoViewer and the attachment sheet get "Send as video message" in the send long-press
menu, for a single gallery video in a chat that allows video messages (not scheduled, not
editing, no paid messages). The menus only mark the video: its VideoEditedInfo gets
roundVideo = true (PhotoViewer through NeoGalleryRound.onViewerSend right after the info
is built, the attachment sheet on the selected entry, restored if nothing was sent).
SendMessagesHelper.prepareSendingMedia hands marked videos to NeoGalleryRound.routeRounds,
which takes them out of the album and, on a background thread, builds the video message
from createCompressionSettings (now public) and the user's edits: the central square of
their crop, at most a minute from their trim start, the side, bitrate and frame rate of the
round video settings. The stock prepareSendingVideo then converts and sends it like a
camera video message (round_message, blurred thumbnail, no caption or grouping).
